 "rationale": "Fixed before any failed goal was read. The unit is the task family, so variants of one specification (b1..b5) and real-world tasks of the same domain never fall on both sides. The frozen test split is never mined into the library (as in harness/harvest.py LIBRARY_SPLITS), so its families are held out. Of the remaining families, two of six are drawn by hash with a fixed salt rather than chosen, so the held-out set does not depend on which goals look easy to close; the draw puts lending (Compound, Euler) and fixed-point (Balancer, Cetus) on the held-out side. Mining reads only runs of mining-set tasks; every measurement of effect is on held-out tasks only.",
